    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe logic itself is in the right place and done well: `toBusinessDay` is the correct home for this rule, the holiday data is cleanly separated from the roll logic, the `while` loop is an idiomatic generalization of the old `if` branches, there's no duplication, and the javadoc was faithfully updated. The one structural issue is placement.\n\n**Finding \u2014 `HOLIDAYS` constant is placed inconsistently with the class's convention (line 375).**\n\nThis class establishes a clear convention: all `private static final` class-level constants live in a grouped block at the very top of the class body (`CITY_CAPACITY`, `DAILY_CAPACITY`, `BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD`, lines 51\u201358), each with a short javadoc, *above* the field declarations and constructor. The new `HOLIDAYS` constant instead sits mid-class at line 375, wedged between `countRegisteredToday()` and `toBusinessDay()`.\n\nA maintainer scanning this file would expect to find all such constants in the top block and would not naturally look for one buried between two methods. For consistency and discoverability, move the `HOLIDAYS` declaration (and its javadoc) up into the existing constants block alongside the other three, leaving `toBusinessDay` as just the method.\n\nThis is the only change needed; everything else about the diff is clean.",
